WEBVTT

00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:11.210
What is that?

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:12.630
That thing spinning in the sky.

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:13.400
Is it a Ferris wheel?

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.250
Can we go on it, Ma'am?

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:19.510
Once you go on, you can never come back.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:22.570
Walk the rest of the way home by yourself.

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:27.230
Ma'am?

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:32.250
<i>Somewhere, neither in this 
life nor the afterlife,</i>

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:37.800
<i>lies Kyoukai, a border world 
between this and the next.</i>

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:41.790
<i>There, it is said, is a great 
"Rinne no Wa," the Ring of Reincarnation,</i>

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:44.090
<i>which channels the flow of life.</i>

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:46.540
Ma'am!

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:48.660
Ma'am!

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.260
Ma'am!

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:54.320
Ma'am!

00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:01.640
You mean "Miss."

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:02.540
Ow, ow.

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:05.170
And you better forget 
everything you saw here.

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:06.260
Rather, you will forget.

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:08.000
Ow, ow.

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:43.960
<i>I thought things would be different 
once I started high school.</i>

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.810
Morning, Mamiya Sakura-san.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:54.510
<i>However, nothing changed.</i>

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:56.500
Hey, you hear me, don't you?

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:58.040
Let's talk.

00:02:58.370 --> 00:02:59.860
Please don't talk to me.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:01.400
Ow...

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:07.620
The Mysterious Classmate

00:03:10.570 --> 00:03:12.210
Everyone, take your seats.

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:16.590
Hey, Sakura-chan, your 
neighbor is absent again.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:18.670
Oh yeah.

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:21.470
I wonder why; it's already May.

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:22.790
Rokudou.

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:24.850
Is Rokudou Rinne absent again?

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:34.550
Looks like my neighbor's here, Miho-chan.

00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:38.690
<i>So this is Rokudou-kun.</i>

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:41.740
<i>But what's up with his weird outfit?</i>

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:43.660
<i>And his hair's bright red.</i>

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:47.030
We'll have to think of something if 
he's going to be absent any more.

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:49.020
Maybe he's refusing school.

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:50.540
He might not come anymore.

00:03:50.990 --> 00:03:53.640
Sakura-chan, what do you mean "he's here"?

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:58.590
<i>Can no one else see him?</i>

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:02.340
<i>Which means... he's a ghost?</i>

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:06.610
<i>Crap, our eyes met.</i>

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:15.560
<i>Dog food?</i>

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:22.190
All right, let's begin the morning homeroom.

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:26.070
<i>Um, what is this?</i>

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:29.150
<i>It has huge eyes and it's always shaking.</i>

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:31.450
<i>Oh, right, a chihuahua.</i>

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:33.570
So-called Chiwatarou,

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:35.680
abandon your earthly regrets

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:38.210
and take to the flow of the 
Rinne no Wa immediately.

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:40.010
Now.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:44.980
It's all right.

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:46.840
Don't be afraid.

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:57.170
<i>H-He got eaten.</i>

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:02.830
You kind of look off somewhere, 
don't you, Sakura-chan?

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:03.620
Is it a habit?

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:05.780
Yeah, I can't fix it.

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:09.230
See you later.

00:05:09.230 --> 00:05:11.000
Okay, bye.

00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:15.580
<i>I thought something would 
be different in high school;</i>

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:20.460
<i>that I might grow up a little 
and stop seeing strange things.</i>

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:23.050
Are you heading home, Mamiya Sakura-san?

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:29.740
Hey, Mamiya Sakura-san.

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:31.640
Hey, come on.

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:38.250
Sakura-chan, he's here.

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:39.900
Rokudou-kun, the guy who sits next to you.

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:46.900
<i>Huh? What about yesterday?</i>

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:48.610
Rokudou, right?

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:51.340
Why are you in a track suit?

00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:53.240
This is from junior high.

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:54.540
You haven't bought a uniform?

00:05:55.590 --> 00:05:57.960
If I bought something so lavish,

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:00.170
I'd go to Hell.

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:02.840
Huh? Are you really p—

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:04.220
I'll go to Hell.

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:06.900
I-I feel bad. Sorry, Rokudou.

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:09.090
Yeah, never say it again.

00:06:11.290 --> 00:06:14.550
Hey, Sakura-chan, have you ever 
talked to Rokudou-kun or anything?

00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:15.400
Not at all.

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:17.140
He's a bit weird, isn't he?

00:06:17.530 --> 00:06:19.940
Hey, Rika-chan is that a new phone?

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:22.150
Yeah, I bought it just last week.

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:23.390
It's cute.

00:06:23.390 --> 00:06:27.280
Y'know, though, I get wrong number calls.

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:28.910
Wrong number?

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:30.060
Every day.

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:33.390
At the same time every day, 
after school. It sucks.

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:34.380
Saying what?

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:35.910
It's some guy I don't know...

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:38.160
<i>"Be behind the gym at four o'clock!"</i>

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:39.760
I don't know his voice,

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:42.390
and I don't remember doing 
anything to get called out.

00:06:43.480 --> 00:06:44.040
<i>Huh?</i>

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:47.050
<i>Something weird just came out of the phone.</i>

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:48.950
Maybe he'll stop eventually.

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:51.220
I hope so.

00:06:51.490 --> 00:06:53.680
But it's too weird! I can't take it!

00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:56.010
What, the phone calls?

00:06:56.010 --> 00:06:58.400
He still calls me, even 
when I block his number.

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:01.730
I called him to complain earlier, and...

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:06.230
<i>"The number you have dialed is not in service."</i>

00:07:06.620 --> 00:07:07.690
I don't believe it!

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:10.840
Could it be a spirit or 
something calling you?

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:12.250
Don't!

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:14.980
Like, a call from

00:07:15.470 --> 00:07:16.550
the afterlife?

00:07:16.550 --> 00:07:17.870
Stop it!

00:07:18.230 --> 00:07:19.790
You should cancel your cont—

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:21.010
I know of someone

00:07:21.930 --> 00:07:24.990
you can talk to about those kinds of things.

00:07:25.600 --> 00:07:27.150
There's a instrument shelter

00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:29.390
in the schoolyard that 
isn't being used anymore.

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:32.260
Write a letter about your problem,

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:37.280
and put it in there along 
with money and an offering.

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:39.770
It's a legend that's been 
passed down in this school.

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:41.200
Have you heard of it?

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:44.610
My sister went to this high school, 
but I never heard about it.

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:46.860
Rika-chan, are you actually 
going to ask for it?

00:07:47.380 --> 00:07:49.010
I have to believe.

00:07:49.010 --> 00:07:51.060
I'm out of options.

00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:52.390
<i>No, you aren't.</i>

00:07:52.390 --> 00:07:54.110
<i>You could try changing 
your number or something.</i>

00:07:57.340 --> 00:07:58.530
Please.

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:05.890
Wait, it just opened by itself!

00:08:05.890 --> 00:08:07.880
The letter and the bread disappeared!

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:11.550
I'm so scared!

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:16.410
Rika-chan dropped her phone.

00:08:20.210 --> 00:08:21.100
Say something!

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:24.800
Mamiya Sakura, was it?

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:26.940
Just who are you?

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:30.570
That's my line, Rokudou Rinne-kun.

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:33.710
Why are you sometimes 
visible and sometimes not?

00:08:33.710 --> 00:08:35.560
What's up with this flashy haori?

00:08:35.560 --> 00:08:36.550
Do you think you're overdressed?

00:08:36.550 --> 00:08:37.750
Don't tug on it.

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:38.530
It's high-quality.

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:41.580
You can't buy your school uniform, 
but you can buy a haori?

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:44.260
This the Haori of the Underworld.

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:46.280
It's an awesome item that essentially 
turns the wearer into a spirit,

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:49.320
giving them the same 
physical essence as a spirit.

00:08:49.790 --> 00:08:52.380
Normal people shouldn't be able 
to see me when I'm wearing it.

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:54.180
Oh yeah?

00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:55.260
I guess I get it, for now.

00:08:55.770 --> 00:08:57.510
Never mind that, what do 
you think you're doing?

00:08:57.510 --> 00:08:58.300
Never mind?

00:08:58.520 --> 00:09:00.710
The legend of the instrument shelter.

00:09:00.710 --> 00:09:02.060
You made that up, didn't you?

00:09:02.610 --> 00:09:04.940
What if I did? I need it to make a living.

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:06.730
A living?

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:09.140
You call tricking people into 
giving you offerings a—

00:09:09.140 --> 00:09:10.300
I'm not tricking them.

00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:11.400
I do what I have to do.

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:13.050
What you have to do?

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:16.280
That phone...

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:17.910
I sense the presence of a spirit that can't

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:19.950
rest in peace because it has 
regrets in the mortal world.

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:22.330
Miho

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:21.810
<i>Hello?</i>

00:09:22.490 --> 00:09:24.960
Are you the one that picked up my phone?

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:28.630
If you don't mind, could you please 
bring it to the café by the station?

00:09:30.950 --> 00:09:34.410
A curse upon you!

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:38.540
That'll stop her from asking for 
her phone back for a while.

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:40.160
Th-That's awful.

00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:41.390
She's persistent.

00:09:41.820 --> 00:09:42.850
A cur—

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:44.220
<i>Be behind the gym at four o'clock!</i>

00:09:47.460 --> 00:09:48.330
He's not here.

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:52.440
Maybe that spirit isn't 
necessarily from this school.

00:09:53.330 --> 00:09:55.570
One thing that's certain is that

00:09:55.570 --> 00:09:58.100
the spirit couldn't meet with the person

00:09:58.100 --> 00:10:01.100
he had called to meet behind the gym at four.

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:05.450
That means he died before he met them, right?

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:10.460
I wonder where they are, 
and where they're calling from.

00:10:10.690 --> 00:10:12.730
The best thing would be to ask him directly.

00:10:12.730 --> 00:10:13.460
Huh?

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:17.730
A tin can phone?

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:24.970
Spirit World Tin Can Phone

00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:20.730
<i>This is a spirit world tin can phone.</i>

00:10:20.730 --> 00:10:23.840
<i>It's a handy tool that lets you 
talk to a spirit of your choice.</i>

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:24.970
<i>70 yen.</i>

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:27.700
Give me the phone number of the querent Rika.

00:10:28.490 --> 00:10:29.450
Sure.

00:10:30.470 --> 00:10:31.570
Thanks.

00:10:31.570 --> 00:10:32.820
Now go home.

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:35.890
But I'd leave you alone here, and...

00:10:35.890 --> 00:10:36.980
Don't worry.

00:10:36.980 --> 00:10:39.860
I mean, you might swipe the phone.

00:10:40.530 --> 00:10:42.150
I'll give it back.

00:10:42.150 --> 00:10:42.870
Really?

00:10:43.470 --> 00:10:47.500
I've decided to never steal or defraud.

00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:49.260
Okay, then.

00:10:49.260 --> 00:10:51.390
Is there nothing I should help with?

00:10:51.980 --> 00:10:53.220
Help?

00:10:53.650 --> 00:10:55.840
You seem to be able to see spirits,

00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:58.220
but you've never exorcised 
one or fought one, have you?

00:10:58.680 --> 00:11:00.630
What happens next is my job.

00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:03.640
Your job?

00:11:05.070 --> 00:11:07.110
To guide restless spirits

00:11:07.110 --> 00:11:10.140
with regrets in the mortal 
world to the Rinne no Wa

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:11.270
and let them be reborn.

00:11:14.680 --> 00:11:15.790
Mamiya Sakura.

00:11:15.790 --> 00:11:16.400
Yes?

00:11:17.620 --> 00:11:19.230
Do you have 10 yen?

00:11:19.770 --> 00:11:21.280
I need change to make a call 
with the tin can phone.

00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:24.160
<i>It's not free?</i>

00:11:29.820 --> 00:11:32.600
<i>The spirit making the wrong number call</i>

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:35.130
<i>is connected to the mortal world 
through querent Rika's phone number.</i>

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:37.570
<i>In other words, by following 
the smartphone number,</i>

00:11:37.570 --> 00:11:40.670
<i>they can meet with the spirit.</i>

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:43.000
Wait, where are we?

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:44.090
The Reidou.

00:11:44.630 --> 00:11:47.250
It connects spirits over time and space.

00:11:47.710 --> 00:11:49.260
I'm going to start the call.

00:11:49.260 --> 00:11:51.190
Huh? O-Okay.

00:11:51.190 --> 00:11:52.210
Ten yen, right?

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:56.390
Hey, it's me.

00:11:56.390 --> 00:11:59.170
<i>Is it you? Be behind the 
gym at four o'clock!</i>

00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:01.820
Give me more 10 yen coins.

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:03.600
We can't reach him if the call gets cut off.

00:12:03.970 --> 00:12:04.910
Fine, fine.

00:12:07.430 --> 00:12:08.910
I'll be there, I swear.

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:09.750
Don't be late!

00:12:10.020 --> 00:12:12.510
<i>That's the spirit making wrong number calls?</i>

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:14.000
Look out!

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:17.300
I'll be there, I swear.

00:12:17.300 --> 00:12:17.920
Don't be late!

00:12:18.390 --> 00:12:19.920
Huh, again?

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:22.700
He can't make it past this spot.

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:24.770
He does the same thing 
over and over, every day,

00:12:25.240 --> 00:12:27.640
so I'm going to give him 
a path to go forward.

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:30.550
With that supposedly high quality, 
so-called Haori of the Underworld?

00:12:30.550 --> 00:12:32.970
The Haori of the Underworld turns 
the wearer into a spirit.

00:12:32.970 --> 00:12:34.190
Flip it inside out, and...

00:12:36.700 --> 00:12:39.910
<i>Make a ghost wear it inside 
out, and they materialize.</i>

00:12:39.910 --> 00:12:43.860
<i>A convenient and fashionable reversible item!</i>

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:45.740
He came out of nowhere!

00:12:46.150 --> 00:12:49.800
This is the best way to move a 
spirit away from where it died.

00:12:50.110 --> 00:12:53.030
And there are no expenses 
or additional costs.

00:12:53.030 --> 00:12:53.920
It's free.

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:55.120
My, what a bargain.

00:12:56.130 --> 00:12:58.750
Let's go, then, mister wrong-number spirit.

00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:02.380
Huh? Where to?

00:13:03.400 --> 00:13:04.880
Behind the gym.

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:06.100
Why?

00:13:06.880 --> 00:13:07.850
Who?

00:13:10.170 --> 00:13:13.280
Apparently you called 
someone out here at four.

00:13:13.690 --> 00:13:14.520
I did?

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:18.960
I think he's forgotten a lot 
from the trauma of the accident.

00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:20.970
He can't be rid of his 
regret unless he finishes

00:13:20.970 --> 00:13:22.320
what he came here to do.

00:13:22.980 --> 00:13:26.110
Even then, it looks like it's been a 
long time since he became a spirit.

00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:29.550
Without some kind of hint, he 
won't be able to rest in peace.

00:13:29.550 --> 00:13:30.910
Oh, there you are.

00:13:31.840 --> 00:13:33.160
Hey, Rokudou.

00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:36.020
Mamiya Sakura, take the 
Haori of the Underworld off of him.

00:13:36.020 --> 00:13:37.160
We don't want him to be seen.

00:13:37.160 --> 00:13:39.880
But a lot of people have 
seen him on the way here.

00:13:40.190 --> 00:13:41.460
Do you have a minute?

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:42.620
I'm busy.

00:13:42.620 --> 00:13:46.260
Hey, Rokudou, you don't have a 
standard school track suit, do you?

00:13:46.730 --> 00:13:49.140
Here, it's a hand-me-down, 
but you can have it.

00:13:51.490 --> 00:13:52.530
What's up?

00:13:52.530 --> 00:13:54.510
Does it bother you that it's a hand-me-down?

00:13:54.920 --> 00:13:55.770
No.

00:13:56.550 --> 00:13:58.770
Th-Thank you.

00:13:59.550 --> 00:14:00.380
<i>Huh?</i>

00:14:00.820 --> 00:14:04.600
<i>He looks like he's really happy.</i>

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:07.040
You'll take it?

00:14:07.080 --> 00:14:08.160
Don't wake me up if this is a dream.

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:09.370
I'm glad.

00:14:09.710 --> 00:14:15.620
Actually, this track suit belonged to 
a classmate when I was a student here.

00:14:16.390 --> 00:14:18.620
He died in an accident.

00:14:19.140 --> 00:14:20.960
<i>So it belongs to a dead person.</i>

00:14:22.740 --> 00:14:25.300
<i>He's definitely reacting to the track suit.</i>

00:14:25.900 --> 00:14:28.940
Um, do you think you can remember something?

00:14:30.820 --> 00:14:34.980
Why do you have a classmate's 
track suit, Suzuki-sensei?

00:14:34.980 --> 00:14:39.230
I accidentally brought that track 
suit home on the day of the accident.

00:14:39.230 --> 00:14:41.100
He was a Suzuki, too, after all.

00:14:42.180 --> 00:14:45.280
He was furious that day, and...

00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:47.650
<i>Come behind the gym, four-o-clock!</i>

00:14:48.060 --> 00:14:51.240
And just before we were supposed 
to meet, he got in the accident.

00:14:52.260 --> 00:14:55.370
I couldn't throw it out.

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:57.580
If Rokudou will wear that for me,

00:14:57.580 --> 00:14:59.120
I'd really appreciate it.

00:15:01.090 --> 00:15:02.460
Wait, Suzuki-kun?!

00:15:02.820 --> 00:15:03.930
Oh yeah.

00:15:03.930 --> 00:15:08.540
I noticed on my way home that 
I had the wrong track suit.

00:15:08.990 --> 00:15:13.380
You Can Do It, Suzuki<3

00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:11.740
The girl I was dating embroidered it for me.

00:15:11.740 --> 00:15:13.390
My precious track suit.

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:15.230
I see no such embroidery.

00:15:15.230 --> 00:15:17.350
What are you doing, 
hiding it with your finger?

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:19.600
You Can Do It, Suzuki <3

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:18.510
There.

00:15:18.510 --> 00:15:19.600
There's no mistake.

00:15:20.030 --> 00:15:21.110
You're right.

00:15:21.110 --> 00:15:22.610
I didn't notice it.

00:15:22.610 --> 00:15:24.060
Good thing, huh, Rokudou-kun?

00:15:24.380 --> 00:15:27.440
His regret was that he couldn't 
get his track suit back.

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:28.490
I'm not sure.

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:30.590
What else could it be?

00:15:30.590 --> 00:15:33.240
Do you <i>actually</i> want that track suit?

00:15:33.570 --> 00:15:36.120
No, I'm just not that easily convinced.

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:42.250
I'd be happy if I could rid the spirit 
of his regret just by letting go of this.

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:46.130
Sensei, please, give this back to him

00:15:47.110 --> 00:15:48.520
with your hands.

00:15:50.310 --> 00:15:51.490
What's wrong, Rokudou?

00:15:51.490 --> 00:15:52.930
You're crying blood.

00:15:53.350 --> 00:15:54.810
No, don't mind me.

00:15:54.810 --> 00:15:56.260
<i>You're seriously regretful.</i>

00:15:57.820 --> 00:15:59.110
Sorry I got them mixed up.

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:00.830
Here, this one's yours.

00:16:04.130 --> 00:16:06.060
My track suit.

00:16:11.720 --> 00:16:13.480
Huh, Suzuki-kun?

00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:15.280
Looks like he can rest in peace.

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:20.210
That's why he kept calling: 
because he couldn't rest.

00:16:20.590 --> 00:16:21.710
Calling?

00:16:21.710 --> 00:16:22.370
Yeah.

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:29.020
The day after Suzuki-kun died, 
I got a weird phone call.

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:32.870
I canceled my number right away!

00:16:34.060 --> 00:16:35.970
<i>That number got passed around and around</i>

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:38.380
<i>until it was assigned to Rika's cell phone</i>

00:16:38.380 --> 00:16:40.640
<i>and the truth was revealed.</i>

00:16:42.320 --> 00:16:45.650
I'm glad the wrong number 
caller can rest in peace.

00:16:46.070 --> 00:16:47.030
Yeah,

00:16:47.580 --> 00:16:49.040
though too bad about the track suit.

00:16:49.670 --> 00:16:51.130
<i>He's still regretting it.</i>

00:16:51.670 --> 00:16:52.610
Stop.

00:16:54.320 --> 00:17:02.540
Spirit Net

00:16:54.750 --> 00:16:56.640
<i>This is a Spirit Net.</i>

00:16:56.640 --> 00:17:01.020
<i>A useful item that captures 
spirits in hiding.</i>

00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:02.540
<i>180 yen.</i>

00:17:04.190 --> 00:17:05.650
That chihuahua.

00:17:05.650 --> 00:17:07.040
Isn't it smaller?

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:07.810
Yeah.

00:17:07.810 --> 00:17:08.790
What's going on?

00:17:09.100 --> 00:17:11.550
Why are you with this guy, 
Sakura-san? What's going on?

00:17:11.550 --> 00:17:13.850
Oh, it's that spirit I see all the time.

00:17:13.850 --> 00:17:15.130
Are you a bound spirit, too?

00:17:15.490 --> 00:17:18.640
You better give up your regrets soon, 
or you'll become an evil spirit.

00:17:18.900 --> 00:17:21.720
An evil spirit? That would suck.

00:17:22.690 --> 00:17:26.040
Mamiya Sakura, how much 
do you have left in your wallet?

00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:27.340
Money?

00:17:27.610 --> 00:17:28.820
Just in case.

00:17:28.820 --> 00:17:31.310
I think about 1,500 yen.

00:17:31.310 --> 00:17:32.990
Are you rich? Are you seriously rich?

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:34.740
Oh yeah?

00:17:34.740 --> 00:17:36.990
So you have a regret in this world, too, huh?

00:17:37.540 --> 00:17:38.780
You're the same as me.

00:17:40.420 --> 00:17:43.050
<i>I was so busy studying while I was alive,</i>

00:17:43.050 --> 00:17:45.290
<i>I'd never even talked to a girl.</i>

00:17:46.110 --> 00:17:49.370
<i>So I really wanted to be friends with a girl.</i>

00:17:49.370 --> 00:17:50.830
<i>I kept talking to them.</i>

00:17:51.530 --> 00:17:53.670
<i>The one person that replied...</i>

00:17:54.360 --> 00:17:55.380
Morning.

00:17:55.830 --> 00:17:57.550
Good morning.

00:17:57.870 --> 00:18:02.190
Mamiya Sakura-san, you were the 
only one that talked to me.

00:18:02.190 --> 00:18:04.930
I thought you were a normal person, so...

00:18:04.930 --> 00:18:07.490
You're the only one that gets me!

00:18:07.490 --> 00:18:09.190
Maybe she'll date me.

00:18:09.190 --> 00:18:11.690
No, she must have feelings for me!

00:18:12.110 --> 00:18:13.180
What should we do?

00:18:13.180 --> 00:18:15.240
Should I force him to rest?

00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:18.790
I'd feel bad for him.

00:18:18.790 --> 00:18:20.490
Don't worry about it.

00:18:20.810 --> 00:18:22.550
I think I'll be okay like this.

00:18:22.550 --> 00:18:24.750
I'd hate not being able to see you anymore.

00:18:25.230 --> 00:18:27.800
Uh, you're kind of mixed up.

00:18:27.800 --> 00:18:29.570
Shoot, he's turned evil.

00:18:29.570 --> 00:18:31.380
An evil spirit? This?

00:18:32.080 --> 00:18:33.220
Go out with me.

00:18:33.220 --> 00:18:33.880
Sorry.

00:18:36.570 --> 00:18:38.130
Give it up and rest.

00:18:38.650 --> 00:18:40.430
It's okay, don't be scared.

00:18:43.680 --> 00:18:45.940
I got rejected!

00:18:52.580 --> 00:18:54.190
Sorry, give me a hand.

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:08.610
<i>What is that?</i>

00:19:13.300 --> 00:19:14.500
We're flying!

00:19:16.020 --> 00:19:17.880
Where are we, Rokudou-kun?

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:19.630
Wait!

00:19:19.630 --> 00:19:20.990
He's chasing us!

00:19:22.950 --> 00:19:25.220
He was bound to this world through

00:19:25.220 --> 00:19:27.640
his infatuation with you, Mamiya Sakura.

00:19:31.850 --> 00:19:35.680
The only way to save him 
was to bring you here.

00:19:41.520 --> 00:19:43.530
S-So...

00:19:44.060 --> 00:19:47.290
C-Can you give me 500 yen?

00:19:47.730 --> 00:19:50.540
In order to make him, 
or rather, them, rest.

00:19:51.510 --> 00:19:52.540
500 yen?

00:19:52.980 --> 00:19:55.650
I knew it, it's too much to ask for.

00:19:58.110 --> 00:20:01.430
No. I'll pay. I'll pay.

00:20:02.170 --> 00:20:03.090
Do what you can with this.

00:20:08.360 --> 00:20:09.770
Thank you.

00:20:11.850 --> 00:20:22.280
Fire Wheel

00:20:12.630 --> 00:20:13.880
<i>This is a Fire Wheel.</i>

00:20:14.260 --> 00:20:16.010
<i>A super-powerful item that</i>

00:20:16.010 --> 00:20:19.210
<i>rends a spirit from its regrets and 
guides them to the Rinne no Wa.</i>

00:20:19.580 --> 00:20:22.280
<i>Its price? Just 500 yen!</i>

00:20:22.700 --> 00:20:26.390
So-called Chiwatarou and 
lovesick bound spirit,

00:20:26.390 --> 00:20:28.870
I hereby rend you both 
from your earthly regrets.

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:31.460
Don't call me that!

00:20:32.190 --> 00:20:33.790
Fire Wheel Fissioning!

00:20:39.430 --> 00:20:41.840
Oh, it wasn't that impressive.

00:20:46.600 --> 00:20:49.890
Now then, you two, get on 
the Rinne no Wa immediately.

00:20:51.670 --> 00:20:53.310
Man, I'm kind of lonely.

00:20:53.630 --> 00:20:54.690
There are girls on it, too.

00:20:54.690 --> 00:20:55.770
What? Oh, really?

00:20:56.120 --> 00:20:56.990
Bye!

00:21:01.220 --> 00:21:05.230
<i>I feel like I've been here before.</i>

00:21:05.580 --> 00:21:06.780
Mamiya Sakura.

00:21:07.860 --> 00:21:10.600
The living must not come here.

00:21:11.070 --> 00:21:14.290
It was an emergency, 
but I'm sorry I brought you here.

00:21:14.880 --> 00:21:19.040
Rokudou-kun, what exactly are you?

00:21:19.730 --> 00:21:25.800
I guide restless spirits with 
earthly regrets to the Rinne no Wa.

00:21:26.250 --> 00:21:27.050
I'm a shinigami.

00:21:27.740 --> 00:21:29.050
A shinigami?

00:21:29.790 --> 00:21:30.840
Kind of thing.

00:21:31.370 --> 00:21:32.410
Kind of thing?

00:21:34.670 --> 00:21:35.850
Here, Rika-chan.

00:21:36.230 --> 00:21:37.920
My cell phone!

00:21:37.920 --> 00:21:39.980
You picked it up for me, Sakura-chan.

00:21:39.980 --> 00:21:41.070
Yeah, I guess.

00:21:41.570 --> 00:21:44.430
I don't think you'll get those 
wrong number calls anymore.

00:21:44.430 --> 00:21:46.750
Huh? Really? Why?

00:21:47.360 --> 00:21:48.630
It's just a feeling.

00:21:56.840 --> 00:21:59.290
I've never seen someone with a 
part-time job making fake flowers.

00:22:00.050 --> 00:22:05.050
<i>Soon, the legend of the instrument 
shelter spread throughout the school.</i>

00:22:05.410 --> 00:22:07.870
So you can just use a 1 yen coin offering.

00:22:07.870 --> 00:22:10.320
Yeah, it worked just fine.

00:22:10.320 --> 00:22:12.430
I guess I'll make a request, too, then.

00:22:17.420 --> 00:22:19.870
So this is the legendary instrument shelter.

00:22:19.870 --> 00:22:22.320
Huh? There's a sign.

00:22:22.320 --> 00:22:25.840
"Cheap out on your offering, 
and you'll be cursed. – Shinigami"?

00:24:00.210 --> 00:24:25.150
Next Episode
Memories of the Red Ring

00:24:00.600 --> 00:24:03.400
Hey, hey, Miho-chan, Sakura-chan, 
let's have cake on our way home.

00:24:03.400 --> 00:24:05.250
I want to go that new café.

00:24:05.250 --> 00:24:06.330
But I might gain weight.

00:24:06.330 --> 00:24:09.260
Don't worry, just make a request 
to the instrument shelter.

00:24:09.260 --> 00:24:12.820
Um, I don't think we should 
rely on it too much.

00:24:12.820 --> 00:24:13.840
Who cares?

00:24:13.840 --> 00:24:15.700
It's just a desperate wish to god.

00:24:15.700 --> 00:24:17.990
Well, to be accurate, a wish to a shinigami.

00:24:17.990 --> 00:24:19.150
Rokudou-kun.

00:24:19.150 --> 00:24:20.790
I'm used to hearing selfish requests.

00:24:20.790 --> 00:24:22.840
Whether I grant them or not is another story.

00:24:23.520 --> 00:24:27.050
Next time on <i>Rin-ne</i>: 
"Memories of the Red Ring."
